This file marks the loopr source tree.

Loopr orchestrates OTHER repos; it never operates on itself. The loopr binary,
when given an effective target directory (CWD by default, `-C <path>` to
override), walks up from the target looking for this file. If found, loopr
refuses to run with a clear error.

Do not delete this file. Do not copy it into target repos. If loopr refuses
your invocation because of this guard, fix the invocation (point `-C` at the
correct target), not the guard.
